1
00:00:00,030 --> 00:00:02,050
A cow eats every meal twice.

2
00:00:02,410 --> 00:00:04,170
It doesn't have four stomachs.

3
00:00:04,170 --> 00:00:05,990
It has one, with four rooms.

4
00:00:06,500 --> 00:00:08,030
Grass goes into the first,

5
00:00:08,120 --> 00:00:10,510
the rumen, a vat as big as a bathtub,

6
00:00:10,510 --> 00:00:14,290
packed with trillions of microbes that break down tough plant fiber.

7
00:00:14,550 --> 00:00:16,470
Then the cow burps the mush back up,

8
00:00:16,470 --> 00:00:17,450
and chews it again.

9
00:00:17,790 --> 00:00:20,530
That's chewing the cud, up to eight hours a day.

10
00:00:20,910 --> 00:00:22,540
The honeycomb room sorts it,

11
00:00:22,540 --> 00:00:24,340
the third squeezes out the water,

12
00:00:24,340 --> 00:00:26,580
and the fourth digests with acid,

13
00:00:26,580 --> 00:00:27,580
just like yours.

14
00:00:27,580 --> 00:00:30,270
So when a cow just stands there chewing,

15
00:00:30,380 --> 00:00:31,633
it's not bored, because
